IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `feg-employee`

-- Fair Entitlements Guarantee Act 2012 -- worked cases, from the seat of the former employee.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text (C2025C00164), never copied from the encoding's output. No scenario life raised this Act; every
-- case is HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- Sam (HYPOTHETICAL) worked for a company from 1 February 2019 at $1,500 a week. An administrator was appointed on
-- 10 March 2026 and took control of the employees; the administrator ended Sam's job on 20 March 2026; the creditors
-- resolved to wind the company up and a liquidator was appointed on 14 April 2026. Sam is an Australian citizen, has
-- lodged a proof of debt, and is owed annual leave, long service leave, notice, redundancy pay and three weeks' wages.
-- The maximum weekly wage is taken as $2,600, an assumed figure: the indexed figure is set under the Regulations, which
-- are not deposited.

§ `cases`

§§ `s 7 -- wages`

#ASSERT `Is this payment wages` `ordinary pay for work done or paid leave taken`
#ASSERT `Is this payment wages` `overtime`
#ASSERT `Is this payment wages` `an allowance`
#ASSERT `Is this payment wages` `another amount my award or agreement identifies separately and makes payable regularly`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this payment wages` `a discretionary payment, such as a bonus`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this payment wages` `a reimbursement`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this payment wages` `a payment of travel or relocation expenses`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this payment wages` `another amount that is not payable on an ongoing basis`

§§ `s 5 -- the wages entitlement period`

-- The administrator took control on 10 March 2026, before the job ended on 20 March: the 13 weeks (91 days) end on
-- 10 March 2026 and begin on 10 December 2025.
#ASSERT `What is my wages entitlement period` (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS `Period` OF (Date 10 12 2025), (Date 10 3 2026)
-- No practitioner in control before the end: the 13 weeks end on 20 March 2026 and begin on 20 December 2025.
#ASSERT `What is my wages entitlement period` (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS `Period` OF (Date 20 12 2025), (Date 20 3 2026)
-- A practitioner who took control after the job ended does not move the end.
#ASSERT `What is my wages entitlement period` (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE (Date 14 4 2026) EQUALS `Period` OF (Date 20 12 2025), (Date 20 3 2026)

§§ `ss 10 to 13 -- eligibility`

-- The arguments, in order: partnership; what happened; the day it happened; employment ended; the day it ended; the day
-- Sam started; the day the first insolvency practitioner was appointed; ended because insolvent; owed; proved; owed
-- before the event; chased before it; status; effective claim; s 556 excluded employee; relative of a bankrupt; recent
-- spouse of a bankrupt; contractor first; the Secretary satisfied under s 12(1)(c); Ansett.
-- Sam, as stated: a liquidator appointed after the administrator ended his job; owed; proved; a citizen; claimed.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: I am eligible for an advance (s 10(1)), if the Secretary is satisfied of the facts I have given`
-- His job had not ended.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) FALSE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: my employment has not ended (s 10(1)(a))`
-- Administration or receivership alone: no insolvency event.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `none of these` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: no insolvency event (a liquidator's appointment or my employer's bankruptcy) has happened on or after 5 December 2012 (s 10(1)(b))`
-- A liquidator appointed on 1 December 2012, before s 10 commenced on 5 December 2012.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 1 12 2012) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: no insolvency event (a liquidator's appointment or my employer's bankruptcy) has happened on or after 5 December 2012 (s 10(1)(b))`
-- A liquidator appointed on 5 December 2012 itself: after the commencement.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 5 12 2012) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: I am eligible for an advance (s 10(1)), if the Secretary is satisfied of the facts I have given`
-- He left on 10 September 2025 for another reason: exactly 6 months before the administrator's appointment on 10 March 2026 is not less than 6 months before.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 10 9 2025) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: my employment did not end because of the insolvency, nor less than 6 months before or after an insolvency practitioner was appointed (s 10(1)(c))`
-- He left on 11 September 2025 for another reason: less than 6 months before.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 11 9 2025) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: I am eligible for an advance (s 10(1)), if the Secretary is satisfied of the facts I have given`
-- He left on 20 March 2026, after the appointment, whatever the reason (s 10(1)(c)(iii)).
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: I am eligible for an advance (s 10(1)), if the Secretary is satisfied of the facts I have given`
-- Nothing owed.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: I am not owed wages, annual leave, long service leave, notice or redundancy pay (s 10(1)(d))`
-- No proof of debt lodged.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: I have not taken reasonable steps to prove my debts in the winding up or bankruptcy (s 10(1)(e))`
-- Owed wages before the liquidation and never chased them.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: I did not take reasonable steps, before the insolvency event, to be paid what I was already owed (s 10(1)(f))`
-- Owed wages before the liquidation and chased them.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: I am eligible for an advance (s 10(1)), if the Secretary is satisfied of the facts I have given`
-- A temporary visa holder when the job ended.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of these` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: when my employment ended I was not an Australian citizen or the holder of a permanent or special category visa (s 10(1)(g))`
-- A New Zealand citizen on a special category visa.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `the holder of a special category visa` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: I am eligible for an advance (s 10(1)), if the Secretary is satisfied of the facts I have given`
-- No effective claim yet.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: I have not made an effective claim (s 10(1)(h), s 14)`
-- A director's relative, an excluded employee under s 556 in the winding up.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: I am excluded as an excluded employee, a relative or a recent spouse or de facto partner of my employer (s 11)`
-- A relative of a bankrupt sole trader.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `my employer became a bankrupt` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: I am excluded as an excluded employee, a relative or a recent spouse or de facto partner of my employer (s 11)`
-- The bankrupt's former de facto partner within the 12 months.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `my employer became a bankrupt` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: I am excluded as an excluded employee, a relative or a recent spouse or de facto partner of my employer (s 11)`
-- A relative of a director of a company in liquidation, but not an excluded employee: s 11(2) is only for a bankrupt employer.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: I am eligible for an advance (s 10(1)), if the Secretary is satisfied of the facts I have given`
-- Hired on 1 December 2025 after contracting, when the Secretary is satisfied the employer could not be expected to pay: within 6 months before the appointment on 10 March 2026.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 12 2025) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: I am excluded as newly employed after working for my employer as a contractor (s 12)`
-- Hired on 1 September 2025 after contracting: more than 6 months before.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 9 2025) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: I am eligible for an advance (s 10(1)), if the Secretary is satisfied of the facts I have given`
-- Hired on 1 December 2025 after contracting, but the Secretary is not satisfied of s 12(1)(c).
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 12 2025) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: I am eligible for an advance (s 10(1)), if the Secretary is satisfied of the facts I have given`
-- An Ansett group employer.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `answered` `no: my employer was within the Special Employee Entitlements Scheme for Ansett Group Employees (s 13)`
-- Employed by a partnership: not covered.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` TRUE `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `employment for a partnership by two or more of the partners is not encoded (s 10(2))`
-- An administration under a s 49 declaration: not covered.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for an advance` FALSE `my employer is in administration and the Minister has declared under s 49 that the Act applies` (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 1 2 2019) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `an employer in administration under a Minister's declaration under s 49 is not encoded`

§§ `s 14 -- claiming`

-- The later of the liquidator's appointment (14 April 2026) and the end of the job (20 March 2026) is 14 April 2026: claim
-- by 14 April 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I claim` (Date 14 4 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 14 4 2027
-- The job ended after the liquidator was appointed: the 12 months run from the end of the job.
#ASSERT `By when must I claim` (Date 14 4 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 30 4 2027
-- A bankrupt employer discharged on 1 January 2027: claim by 31 December 2026 (s 14(3)).
#ASSERT `By when must I claim` (Date 14 4 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS Date 31 12 2026
-- Discharged after the 12 months: the 12 months govern.
#ASSERT `By when must I claim` (Date 14 4 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 1 2028) EQUALS Date 14 4 2027
-- An event on 29 February 2028: the 12 months end on 28 February 2029.
#ASSERT `By when must I claim` (Date 29 2 2028) (Date 1 2 2028) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 28 2 2029

#ASSERT `Is my claim effective` (Date 14 4 2027) (Date 14 4 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my claim effective` (Date 15 4 2027) (Date 14 4 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my claim effective` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 14 4 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- An earlier GEERS claim for the same job makes the claim ineffective (s 14(4)), unless GEERS rejected it because the
-- insolvency event came before 5 December 2012 (s 14(5)).
#ASSERT NOT `Is my claim effective` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 14 4 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my claim effective` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 14 4 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE

§§ `Part 3 -- the amount`

-- Sam: annual leave $6,000; long service leave $9,000; 4 weeks' pay in lieu of notice, $6,000 (under the 5-week limit of
-- $7,500, s 22); redundancy pay of 10 weeks, $15,000, for 7 years (under the limit of 4 x $1,500 x 7 = $42,000, s 23).
-- Wages for the 13-week period: 13 x $1,500 = $19,500, PAYG on them $3,900 (HYPOTHETICAL figure); he was paid $12,000
-- after tax for 10 of the weeks. Wages: $19,500 - $3,900 - $12,000 = $3,600 (ss 24, 19). His rate is under the maximum
-- weekly wage, so ss 26 and 27 change nothing. Total: 6,000 + 9,000 + 6,000 + 15,000 + 3,600 = $39,600 (s 16).
GIVEN `the day of the insolvency event` IS A DATE
      `offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `later redundant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Secretary's reduction` IS A NUMBER
      `debts` IS A NUMBER
      `nil` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid for annual leave` IS A NUMBER
      `paid for notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`Sam's advance` MEANS
    `How much is my advance` FALSE 2600 1500 6000 9000 6000 15000 7 19500 13 TRUE 1500 FALSE 3900 `paid for annual leave` 0 `paid for notice` 0 12000 `the day of the insolvency event` `offer` `later redundant` `Secretary's reduction` `debts` `nil`

#ASSERT `Sam's advance` (Date 14 4 2026) FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 39600
-- $2,000 already paid towards the annual leave: $4,000 for it, $37,600 in all.
#ASSERT `Sam's advance` (Date 14 4 2026) FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 2000 0 EQUALS `answered` 37600
-- $7,000 already paid towards the notice, more than its $6,000: nil for it, not less (s 19(1)(b)), $33,600 in all.
#ASSERT `Sam's advance` (Date 14 4 2026) FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0 7000 EQUALS `answered` 33600
-- He owes the company $1,000 and the Secretary reduces the advance by it: $38,600 (s 17).
#ASSERT `Sam's advance` (Date 14 4 2026) FALSE FALSE 1000 1000 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 38600
-- A reduction of $5,000 for a $1,000 debt is limited to the debt: $38,600.
#ASSERT `Sam's advance` (Date 14 4 2026) FALSE FALSE 5000 1000 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 38600
-- The Secretary reduces it to nil because the liquidator expects to pay in full within 112 days (s 18).
#ASSERT `Sam's advance` (Date 14 4 2026) FALSE FALSE 0 0 TRUE 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 0
-- s 16(2): an insolvency event of 1 March 2014, and the buyer offered him the same job within 14 days: no notice or
-- redundancy amount, $18,600. Not from 1 July 2014 (s 16(4)); not if the buyer later made him redundant (s 16(3)).
#ASSERT `Sam's advance` (Date 1 3 2014) TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 18600
#ASSERT `Sam's advance` (Date 1 7 2014) TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 39600
#ASSERT `Sam's advance` (Date 1 3 2014) TRUE TRUE 0 0 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 39600

-- A higher earner (HYPOTHETICAL) on $3,250 a week; maximum weekly wage $2,600, so s 26 counts 2,600/3,250 = 0.8 of each
-- entitlement. Annual leave $13,000 -> $10,400. Notice of 6 weeks, $19,500 -> $15,600, limited to 5 x $2,600 = $13,000
-- (s 22). Redundancy of 16 weeks, $52,000 -> $41,600, limited to 4 x $2,600 x 3 years = $31,200 (s 23). Wages: a regular
-- rate over the maximum, so s 27(2): 13 weeks x $2,600 = $33,800, less PAYG $8,000 (HYPOTHETICAL), less $20,000 paid
-- after tax: $5,800. Total: 10,400 + 0 + 13,000 + 31,200 + 5,800 = $60,400.
#ASSERT `How much is my advance` FALSE 2600 3250 13000 0 19500 52000 3 42250 13 TRUE 3250 FALSE 8000 0 0 0 0 20000 (Date 14 4 2026) FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 60400
-- Employed by a partnership: not covered.
#ASSERT `How much is my advance` TRUE 2600 1500 6000 9000 6000 15000 7 19500 13 TRUE 1500 FALSE 3900 0 0 0 0 12000 (Date 14 4 2026) FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `employment for a partnership by two or more of the partners is not encoded (s 10(2))`

-- s 27 on its own. A casual (HYPOTHETICAL) with no rate for regular work, employed 6.5 weeks of the period, wages
-- $19,500: average $3,000 a week, over $2,600, so 6.5 x $2,600 = $16,900 (s 27(3), (5), (6)).
#ASSERT `the basic amount for wages (ss 24, 27)` 2600 19500 6.5 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 16900
-- The same wages with a $1,500 regular rate: s 27(2) does not apply, but the Secretary is satisfied there was no regular
-- pattern, and the average is over the maximum: s 27(4), $16,900.
#ASSERT `the basic amount for wages (ss 24, 27)` 2600 19500 6.5 TRUE 1500 TRUE 0 EQUALS 16900
-- A $1,500 regular rate and a regular pattern: no cap, $19,500.
#ASSERT `the basic amount for wages (ss 24, 27)` 2600 19500 6.5 TRUE 1500 FALSE 0 EQUALS 19500
-- No regular rate, wages $13,000 over 6.5 weeks: average $2,000, no cap, $13,000.
#ASSERT `the basic amount for wages (ss 24, 27)` 2600 13000 6.5 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 13000

§§ `ss 38, 40, 41 -- review`

-- A notice of decision dated 1 June 2026: apply to the Secretary by 29 June 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for review` (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS Date 29 6 2026
#ASSERT `Where can I take the decision` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `first ask the Secretary to review it, within 28 days of the notice (s 38); the Tribunal reviews only the decision made on that review (s 40(1))`
#ASSERT `Where can I take the decision` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `first ask the Secretary to review it, within 28 days of the notice (s 38); the Tribunal reviews only the decision made on that review (s 40(1))`
#ASSERT `Where can I take the decision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I may apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal for review of the decision made on the Secretary's review (s 40(1))`
#ASSERT `Where can I take the decision` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `I may apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal, but it cannot review the Secretary's reduction for my debts to my employer (s 41)`

§§ `s 34 -- repaying`

-- Sam's $39,600 advance; a director later pays him $5,000 towards his redundancy pay: he owes the Commonwealth $5,000.
#ASSERT `How much must I repay` 39600 5000 `someone else, such as my employer, a director or a buyer of the business` 0 0 EQUALS 5000
-- If the Commonwealth has already recovered $36,000 in the winding up, the debt is limited to $39,600 - $36,000 = $3,600.
#ASSERT `How much must I repay` 39600 5000 `someone else, such as my employer, a director or a buyer of the business` 36000 0 EQUALS 3600
-- And after an earlier s 34 debt of $2,000 as well: $39,600 - $38,000 = $1,600.
#ASSERT `How much must I repay` 39600 5000 `someone else, such as my employer, a director or a buyer of the business` 36000 2000 EQUALS 1600
-- A dividend from the liquidator creates no s 34 debt (s 34(1)(c)(ii)).
#ASSERT `How much must I repay` 39600 5000 `the liquidator or bankruptcy trustee` 0 0 EQUALS 0
